norma — NFS server I/O monitor

This repository is a downstream development of a 2026 NFSD VFS
adaptation of two projects. It is not a release by the upstream projects.
The adaptation's MIT notice is preserved in licenses/rocky8-adaptation-MIT.

nfstop: MIT ORCD / orcd-ebpf-tools, Copyright (c) 2025 mit-orcd, MIT.
  https://github.com/mit-orcd/orcd-ebpf-tools/tree/main/nfstop
  Original license: licenses/nfstop-MIT.

nfsdtop: The FrauBSD Project, Copyright (c) 2020-2021, BSD 2-Clause.
  https://github.com/FrauBSD/nfsdtop
  Original license: licenses/nfsdtop-BSD-2-Clause.
  The bpftrace backend retains BSD-2-Clause.

New shared frontend, layout resolver, documentation and build tools are MIT.
The native BPF program is offered under MIT OR GPL-2.0 and declares the
kernel-facing BPF license "Dual MIT/GPL".

Go runtime and dependency licenses are included in licenses/go-dependencies.
The original dependency lockfile is retained, including some upstream UI
modules which are no longer directly used. Build-tool dependencies are included.
libbpf helper declarations are used at build time via system development
headers (LGPL-2.1 OR BSD-2-Clause); no libbpf shared library is required at runtime.

The interface is inspired by iftop. No iftop source code is included.

Release architecture: Linux x86_64. norma is a static Go executable with native
eBPF and bpftrace backends. Selecting bpftrace invokes the separately installed
bpftrace runtime.
